# Long context, any task, and no sidecar model to download.
#
# Long context (10k+), any task — MTP, and no sidecar model to download.
#
# A DFlash2 sidecar keeps its own KV cache over the full context and re-runs up
# to n-max times per verification step, so its cost grows with context. MTP's
# nextn layer reuses the target's state and never pays that. The ranking
# genuinely inverts: DFlash2 wins short, MTP wins long.
#
#   Radeon 8060S at ~31k context of real C source:
#   bare                12.20 t/s
#   this preset         36.07 t/s on verbatim reproduction (97.5% acceptance)
#                       20.54 t/s on prose about the same code
#
# REQUIRES a model with an MTP / nextn head. The draft context is built from the
# target itself (ctx_type = MTP), so a model without one cannot start in this
# mode at all — it fails loudly rather than falling back.
#
# Keep n-max tight. The adaptive controller maximises accepted tokens, not
# throughput, and for MTP those diverge: later nextn layers are less accurate
# while draft cost stays linear in n. With a DFlash2 sidecar the picture
# reverses and n-max 7 is right — see dflash-fp4.
LLAMA_ARG_N_GPU_LAYERS=999
LLAMA_ARG_FLASH_ATTN=on
LLAMA_ARG_CTX_SIZE=32768
LLAMA_ARG_UBATCH=512
LLAMA_ARG_BATCH=2048
LLAMA_ARG_JINJA=1

LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_TYPE=draft-mtp
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_ADAPTIVE=1
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MIN=2
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MAX=4
